# Implementation Plan: Visual Engine Stability Fix (Iteration 2)

The previous attempt to fix the matrix rendering and 3D canvas failed because of an off-by-one logic error in the character scanner and persistent WebGL texture allocation racing.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - I am rewriting the `EquationParser.ts` scanner to correctly handle the boundary between LaTeX environment braces and tag closure markers.
> - I will stabilize the `Canvas3DRenderer.tsx` by deferred initialization and explicit WebGL context handling.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] Engine Stability

#### [MODIFY] [EquationParser.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/engine/EquationParser.ts)
- Fix the off-by-one error in the `segmentEquation` loop. The scanner must check for tag closure `}}` ONLY when internal math braces are already balanced.
- Ensure that the brace level is updated correctly *before* checking for the end-of-tag marker.

#### [MODIFY] [EquationRenderer.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/renderers/EquationRenderer.tsx)
- Surround math segments with explicit `$ ... $` delimiters if they contain complex LaTeX environments to assist KaTeX in identifying math-mode boundaries.
- Add additional diagnostic logging to track segments that fail to render.

#### [MODIFY] [Canvas3DRenderer.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/renderers/Canvas3DRenderer.tsx)
- Stabilize the MathBox context by deferring initialization until the parent container has a non-zero width/height via a `ResizeObserver`.
- Simplify the axes to avoid the common `glTexSubImage2DRobustANGLE` texture crash associated with MathBox labels.

